infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title Diagnose stale data — server first, client last
  desc Name the culprit layer before you touch code; each layer has exactly one right lever
  sequences
    - label Step 1 — Is the route static?
      desc Build output: a circle means static. If static, the Full Route Cache serves build-time HTML — set revalidate or force-dynamic.
    - label Step 2 — Is the fetch cached?
      desc On Next 14 a bare fetch defaults to force-cache in the deploy-proof Data Cache. Give it a revalidate window, tags, or no-store.
    - label Step 3 — Does the mutation invalidate?
      desc A write that never calls revalidatePath/revalidateTag leaves every cache intact — the single most common omission.
    - label Step 4 — Stale in only one tab?
      desc Server is fresh via curl, back-navigation shows old data — the client Router Cache; fix in step 3 or router.refresh().
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
